     There is no timeout for divine anger; waiting will not accomplish
anything here.  And sacrificing wimpy monsters will not appease an
angry god either, no matter how many of them you offer.  Ditto for
killing hostile monsters to improve your alignment.  You have to
sacrifice tougher monsters.  Usually one will be enough, although in
the case described in this thread where he kept praying after the god
was angry, the resulting anger would be much higher than usual and
require more than one tough monster sacrifice.  Altar camping can
work, but only if you're deep enough to have a tough monster show up.
Polymorph could be helpful here.

     The quantification of "tough monster" is no doubt in one or
another of the spoilers.  It is the same for lawfuls and neutrals but
higher level (in other words, harder) for chaotics.  That's why using
a helm of opposite alignment to temporarily switch from chaotic to
lawful could be helpful in this situation.


